From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 4evy <git@evy.pink>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 1970 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] redate: align the revision picker with native TUIs

Use a borderless title/main/status layout with stable checked markers and
a full-row focus highlight so graph glyphs only describe topology. Keep
the focused revision timestamp in the title bar, make key hints
responsive, and add select-all, boundary navigation, anchored Shift range
selection, and the standard c-to-confirm binding.

Present the proposed timestamp as prefilled editable input with arrow-key
navigation instead of describing it as a default. Share TUI helpers with
arrange and cover the interaction and responsive layouts with tests.
